# MECHANISM PIN — an assert made AFTER a query must still answer the stratified model.
#
# Fixture INLINE (mechanism pin): the subject is the ENGINE's incremental
# re-saturation, not any particular knowledge base.
#
# THE TRAP THIS CLOSES. Since 2026-08-16 a query builds a saturation, and an insert
# inside that saturation's dependency cone is FOLDED IN rather than recomputed. A fold
# can only ADD tuples, so it is sound only while nothing the delta reaches is read under
# `~` — growth through a negated condition SHRINKS the model. The first version of that
# refusal checked only the DELTA's own relations. That catches the one-hop case and
# misses every longer one: below, `judge` is not read under `~` anywhere, but one
# derivation step later `clean` is, and `free` must LOSE the conclusion the earlier query
# gave it. The fold kept it, and `free(Ada)` answered TRUE where the model says FALSE —
# a definitive wrong verdict, reported by a downstream pin suite on 2026-08-17.
#
# Ordering is the whole point: querying `free` BEFORE the insert is what puts it in the
# saturation. Assert first and every build has always been correct, which is why this
# needs to be a pin and not a comment.

all $x: judge(Court, $x) -> clean($x).
all $x: person($x) & ~clean($x) -> free($x).
all $x: free($x) -> travel($x).
person(Ada).

# ── BEFORE THE INSERT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nothing derives `clean(Ada)`, so the negated guard passes.
? free(Ada).
# => TRUE

? travel(Ada).
# => TRUE

# ── THE INSERT, TWO HOPS BELOW THE GUARD ─────────────────────────────────────
judge(Court, Ada).

? clean(Ada).
# => TRUE

# ── AFTER THE INSERT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `clean(Ada)` now holds, so `~clean($x)` fails and `free` is no longer derivable.
# FALSE here is closed-world non-entailment, exactly as it would be on a KB loaded
# in this order from the start.
? free(Ada).
# => FALSE

# And the consumer of `free` must agree with it in the SAME process. A stale `free`
# beside a recomputed `travel` is mutually inconsistent under `free -> travel`, which
# is what rules out reading the stale answer as some intended monotone semantics.
? travel(Ada).
# => FALSE

:expect-pins 5
